{"family": "gimm_vfi", "task": "interpolation", "name": "GIMM-VFI", "plain": "GIMM-VFI (GIMM-VFI-R and its perceptual GIMM-VFI-R-P, Guo et al., NeurIPS 2024): makes the frame at any time between two video frames from a learned continuous motion field (RAFT flow), for slow motion and higher frame rates. Non-commercial code and weights (S-Lab License 1.0).", "summary": "GIMM-VFI (Guo et al., NeurIPS 2024), the RAFT-based GIMM-VFI-R: arbitrary-time video frame interpolation. RAFT estimates the flow between both frames in both directions; a generalizable implicit motion model (a SIREN MLP on time and position, conditioned on the forward-splatted flow latents) predicts the flow at the requested time; an AMT-style decoder refines it with the bidirectional feature correlation and blends both warped frames. Any time in [0, 1]. `gimm-vfi-r` is trained for accuracy, `gimm-vfi-r-p` adds an LPIPS loss for sharper, perceptually better frames.", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/GSeanCDAT/GIMM-VFI", "upstream_commit": "dbc56449994a3c2e045d46fd46bed570239913f8", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "Generalizable Implicit Motion Modeling for Video Frame Interpolation", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.08680", "date": "2024-07-11", "venue": "NeurIPS 2024", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["raft_flow", "cudnn_hacc"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [], "outputs": [{"name": "frame", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": [], "task_io": "Input: two RGB images (consecutive frames). Output: the frame between them at `timestep` (0.5 by default; 0 = the first, 1 = the second), RGB in [0, 1].", "install": {"extras": ["nc"], "noncommercial_weights": ["gimm-vfi-r", "gimm-vfi-r-p"]}, "variants": [{"id": "gimm-vfi-r", "released": null, "added_